    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d380">

                <pb facs="0914" n="874" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg874"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">886A.2553/12–2754: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 380<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in Saudi
                        Arabia</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d380-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-12-27T15:39:00-05:00">December 27, 1954—3:39
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>280. For your information Duce
                    Aramco told Department today that Board
                    Directors met New York December 22 and decided as compromise measure to deal
                    with Onassis problem it may offer place some Aramco tankers under Saudi flag provided that (1) SAG enacts suitable shipping laws and (2) Article 4
                    of Onassis Agreement concerning preferences be eliminated. Aramco querying field for comment. Duce emphasized decision not final and that
                    some Directors still have considerable misgivings this undertaking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
